# 🧮 8-Bit Calculator: Full Custom RTL-to-GDSII ASIC Flow

[![License: MIT](https://img.shields.io/badge/License-MIT-yellow.svg)](https://opensource.org/licenses/MIT)
[![Verilog](https://img.shields.io/badge/Language-Verilog-blue.svg)](#)
[![Physical Design](https://img.shields.io/badge/Flow-RTL_to_GDSII-orange.svg)](#)

## 📌 Project Overview
This repository documents the complete **RTL to GDSII** physical design flow of an **8-Bit Calculator**. Moving beyond frontend digital logic, this project demonstrates the transformation of behavioral Verilog code into a fully routable, manufacturable silicon layout. 

The calculator features a robust ALU (Arithmetic Logic Unit) capable of handling 8-bit operands, processing fundamental arithmetic and bitwise logic operations, and managing status flags (Carry, Zero, Overflow). This project serves as a comprehensive case study in modern ASIC design methodologies, utilizing standard cell libraries and automated synthesis/routing tools.

---

## 📐 Architecture & Features

### Core Specifications
* **Data Width:** 8-bit Input/Output Datapath.
* **Control Unit:** Custom state machine for instruction decoding.
* **Supported Operations:**
  * **Arithmetic:** `ADD`, `SUB`, `MUL`, `DIV` (Optional based on implementation)
  * **Logical:** `AND`, `OR`, `XOR`, `NAND`, `NOR`, `NOT`
  * **Shifting:** `Logical Shift Left (LSL)`, `Logical Shift Right (LSR)`
* **Flags:** Zero `(Z)`, Carry `(C)`, Overflow `(V)`, Negative `(N)`.

